      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Change-of-Coordinates Matrix Given a Linear Connection Between Two Bases",
      "kp_id": "e-4832"
    },
    "q-81825": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81825",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}.$ \nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} & =3{b}_{3}-{b}_{1}+{b}_{2}, \\\\ {c}_{2} & =4{b}_{2}-5{b}_{1}, \\\\ {c}_{3} & =2{b}_{1}+3{b}_{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand  the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}a & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & b & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The coordinates of the vectors in $C$ relative to the basis $B$ are\n\n$$\n[{c}_{1}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{2}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,[{c}_{3}]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, $a=-1,$ $b=4,$ and $c=3.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
