    "q-81857": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81857",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $C$ to the basis $B$ is given by\n${P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ Find the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$  .",
      "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{C\\to B}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C} & ={P}_{C\\to B}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}-6 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-6)\\cdot 4-(-5)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81857-a",
