    "q-81855": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81855",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from the basis $B$ to the basis $C$ is given by \n${P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}].$\nFind the change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$  .",
      "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is the inverse of the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$ Therefore, we simply need to find the inverse of the given matrix.\n\nComputing the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{C\\to B} & ={P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & -7 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-5)-(-7)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-81855-a",
